# Phase 5 (CTRLO-WIDER-F): the nine emoji bases of the family a terminal
# draws wider (U+261D, U+26F9, U+270C, U+270D, U+1F3CB, U+1F3CC, U+1F574,
# U+1F575, U+1F590) each with a skin-tone modifier, in an answer: a short
# line, then each at the margin -- placed so that xfx's named form
# (`\u{XXXX}` and the modifier) ends on the row's last cells, before
# `TAIL5678`, then 100 `w` and `END`, so each is two rows on both sides
# (fx's first row ends `TAIL5678` by its count, xfx's at the name). A
# second answer: two modifier sequences on bases outside the
# family (U+1F46F, U+1F93C with U+1F3FB: tmux 3.7b draws both four cells,
# `approval_view`'s measured cases) at the margin, the short line in a
# code panel and in a table's cell. fx counts a base and its modifier as
# one RGI sequence, two cells. `wire` keeps every byte written.
gateway p5-ctrlo-wider-mod-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
keep
until shown Run /help for commands
type go
wait 1
key Enter
until shown END-ONE
until gone Generating (
snap answer
wire answer
type more
wait 1
key Enter
until shown END-TWO
until gone Generating (
snap more
wire more
gwlog
